  <header><div class="shell topbar"><a class="brand" href="https://alvaro-ncaa-research-review.alv-mendizabal.chatgpt.site/"><span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">SEL</span>Sports Edge Lab</a><nav class="nav" aria-label="Main"><a href="#historical">Results</a><a href="#current">Coverage</a><a href="#engineering">Engineering</a><a class="optional" href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab">GitHub ↗</a></nav></div></header>
  <main class="shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div><div class="eyebrow">NCAA evidence review · __REVIEW_DATE__</div><h1 id="page-title">Forecast quality.<br>Visible limits.</h1><p>Different objectives produce different leaders. Explore the probabilities, point errors and uncertainty behind a separately evaluated college basketball track.</p><div class="league-pill" id="league-label">__TITLE__</div></div><aside class="hero-aside"><strong>One cohort. A clear comparison.</strong><p>Historical results below describe development-exposed research. The current season must build its own record of saved, timestamped forecasts.</p><a href="../__SIBLING__/index.html" class="league-pill">Explore __SIBLING_LABEL__ →</a></aside></section>
    <div class="status-strip"><div><strong>Latest run stopped at the source handoff.</strong><span id="attempt-summary"></span></div><a href="#execution">See the work ↓</a></div>

    <section class="section" id="execution" aria-labelledby="execution-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Latest measured execution</div><h2 id="execution-title">Completed work. Measured limits.</h2></div><p id="execution-intro"></p></div>
      <div class="run-metrics" id="run-metrics"></div>
      <div class="execution-grid"><article class="panel"><h3>Where the elapsed time went</h3><p class="subtle">Measured across both NCAA leagues. Admission and fixtures are separate from the scientific workflow.</p><div class="time-bar" id="time-bar" role="img"></div><div class="time-legend" id="time-legend"></div><p class="table-note" id="resource-note"></p></article><article class="panel"><h3>Stage evidence</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table class="phase-table"><caption id="stage-caption"></caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="phase-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">Stage counts reflect the authenticated owner evidence. A failed or unstarted stage receives no completion credit. Earlier committed fits and captured observations remain preserved. Research and exact official coverage remain incomplete.</p></article></div>
    </section>
    <div class="snapshot-note" id="readback-note"><strong>B044 verified earlier bytes; it created no new scientific credit.</strong><p id="readback-copy"></p><p id="prepared-copy"></p></div>
    <div class="snapshot-note" id="recent-study"><strong>Preserved B043 scientific work</strong><p id="recent-study-copy"></p><details><summary>Inspect the dated B043 stages</summary><div class="data-scroll"><table class="phase-table"><caption>B043 stage outcomes remain separate from B044</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="recent-phase-table"></tbody></table></div></details></div>
    <div class="snapshot-note" id="preserved-study"><strong>Preserved B033 historical study</strong><span id="preserved-study-copy"></span><details style="margin-top:10px"><summary>Inspect the prior stage evidence</summary><div class="data-scroll"><table class="phase-table"><caption>Prior B033 stages; reused fits remain separate from new fits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Elapsed</th></tr></thead><tbody id="history-phase-table"></tbody></table></div></details></div>
    <section class="section" id="historical" aria-labelledby="historical-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / Historical evidence</div><h2 id="historical-title">Choose the question first.</h2></div><p>The same pooled selection is shown in each season. A seasonal view changes the evaluation window; it does not choose a new winner.</p></div>
      <div class="filters"><label for="objective">Objective<select id="objective"><option value="probability">Win probability</option><option value="accuracy">Winner accuracy</option><option value="margin">Point margin</option><option value="total">Total points</option></select></label><label for="season">Evaluation window<select id="season"><option value="pooled">Both historical seasons</option><option value="2025">2024–25</option><option value="2026">2025–26</option></select></label><div class="selection-note" id="selection-note"></div></div>
      <div class="metrics" id="metrics" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <div class="chart-grid"><div class="panel"><h3 id="chart-title">Reliability, in ten bins.</h3><p class="subtle" id="chart-subtitle"></p><div id="chart"></div><div class="legend" id="chart-legend"></div><p class="table-note" id="chart-note"></p></div><div class="panel"><h3 id="table-title">Objective-specific selections</h3><p class="subtle">Public IDs preserve the result without exposing private model recipes.</p><div class="data-scroll"><table id="model-table"><caption id="table-caption"></caption><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note" id="table-note"></p></div></div>
      <p class="qualification">The two seasons selected these models after evaluation. They are development-exposed, retrospective comparisons. Historical feature releases use a declared 24-hour assumption; full official-season completeness and prospective performance are not established.</p>
      <div class="panel tradeoff" id="tradeoff"><div><div class="eyebrow">Probability versus accuracy</div><h3>Point estimates tell only part of the story.</h3><p>The probability selection is compared with the accuracy selection on identical games. Whole weeks are resampled within each season, 2,000 times. Intervals describe this exposed selection; they are not adjusted for model search.</p></div><div id="tradeoff-values"></div></div>
    </section>
    <div class="snapshot-note"><strong>Your complete private game report</strong><p>Open every supplied game, forecast reconstruction, captured price and unresolved market record in the browser-only viewer. Missing forecasts and quotes stay visible. The report file is never published or uploaded.</p><a class="league-pill" href="https://alvaro-ncaa-research-review.alv-mendizabal.chatgpt.site/private-report/index.html">Open private game report →</a></div>
    <section class="section" id="current" aria-labelledby="current-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / 2026–27 monitoring</div><h2 id="current-title">A new season needs new evidence.</h2></div><p>B043 completed source capture, original reconstruction, current monitoring and native replay. Durable pre-study scorecards survived its injury-checkpoint failure. Earlier historical scores and dated current comparisons remain preserved.</p></div>
      <div class="snapshot-note"><strong id="inventory-age"></strong><span>Source candidates include unmatched official records and possible cross-source duplicates. The count is not a reconciled physical-game denominator. Publishing this review does not refresh source observations.</span></div>
      <div class="panel"><h3>Visible coverage, with its denominator</h3><div class="coverage-grid" id="coverage-counts"></div><p class="table-note" id="week-counts"></p><p class="table-note" id="official-counts"></p><p class="table-note">Unknown phase, opponent division and exact start times, along with possible duplicate records, still need reconciliation. Missing model or quote evidence must not erase an observed game.</p></div>
      <div class="track-grid" style="margin-top:18px"><article class="track"><span class="badge">ORIGINAL · PARAMETERS PRESERVED</span><h3>Frozen-original reconstruction</h3><p id="original-copy"></p><div class="track-footer"><span>Original as-issued credit: <strong>0</strong></span><span>Earlier paired metrics: <strong>preserved below</strong></span></div></article><article class="track"><span class="badge">CURRENT RESEARCH · SEPARATE STREAMS</span><h3>Chronological reconstruction</h3><p id="current-model-copy"></p><div class="track-footer"><span>Pre-study metrics: <strong>Recovered</strong></span></div></article></div>
      <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px" id="issue-recovery"><h3>Existing issues, independently authenticated</h3><p class="coverage-copy" id="issue-recovery-copy"></p><p class="table-note">Research issue rows repeat targets and streams within games. They are not settled wagers, independent game counts or a measured performance improvement. Original issue bytes and timestamps remain unchanged.</p></div>
      <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px"><h3>Separate update clocks</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table><caption>Acquisition, quote and review clocks retain their own meanings.</caption><thead><tr><th>Clock</th><th>Recorded time</th></tr></thead><tbody id="freshness-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note" id="freshness-note"></p></div>
      <div class="panel providers"><h3>Collect broadly. Compare at the right clock.</h3><div class="data-scroll"><table><caption>Latest display coverage and forecast-eligible comparison coverage are separate.</caption><thead><tr><th>Provider</th><th class="provider-product">Product scope</th><th>Latest display</th><th>Eligible comparison</th></tr></thead><tbody id="provider-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="gap-note">A captured price can be displayed even when its game has no qualified model forecast. Latest observed, source-supported pre-tip, actually captured before tip, T-120 and T-60 prices remain distinct. A late or recovered display quote cannot become an earlier model input, issue or executable profit. No current-season market advantage or ROI is established here.</p></div>
      <div class="panel providers" id="current-paired-review"><h3>Preserved earlier frozen-original comparison</h3><p class="subtle" id="current-paired-note"></p><div class="data-scroll" id="current-paired-table"></div><p class="gap-note" id="current-paired-disagreements"></p></div>
      <div class="panel providers" id="latest-current-comparison"><h3>Preserved dated comparison · B043 pre-study</h3><p class="subtle" id="latest-paired-note"></p><div class="data-scroll" id="latest-paired-table"></div><p class="gap-note" id="latest-paired-disagreements"></p></div>
      <div class="panel" style="margin-top:18px" id="durable-report"><h3>Baseline reports survived the research failure.</h3><p class="coverage-copy" id="durable-report-copy"></p><p class="table-note">The checkpoint counts 46,525 game/model rows; the viewer adds four unresolved source rows, giving 46,529. These are model/version rows, not physical games. All 296 previously scored original games retain identical predictions and outcomes; growth to 329 scored games changes the aggregate population without improving frozen weights.</p></div>
      <details class="source-details"><summary>What failed, what completed, and what remains preserved</summary><p>B044 subsequently stopped at the first source-refresh handoff because its acquisition consumer did not accept the authenticated predecessor release. It completed zero of sixteen stages and committed no new model fits or forecasts. B045 prepares an exact producer-consumer preflight and acquisition handoff repair; the earlier missing-clock repair and scientific outcomes remain dated evidence.</p><p>B043 completed nine of sixteen stages and preserved baseline reports before injury research. An unknown prediction-row label clock reached strict checkpoint JSON as NaT, stopping the injury stage before completed ablations. B044 normalizes missing membership clocks to null without inventing dates or weakening training-label release rules. Historical archive, in-game acquisition and market-path research were not reached; no scientific gain is inferred from repair tests.</p><p>B042 completed nine stages before its injury base verifier encountered a last-bit difference between two floating-point reductions. The B043 repair matches the original producer exactly and retains the equality guard; it does not rewrite predictions or loosen cutoffs. The injury study produced no new challenger fits. Five later stages, including final issue reconciliation and scorecards, were not started.</p><p>The B041 owner remains a separate setup failure: independent predecessor queues reused one progress counter, and the monotonic guard stopped setup before science. B040 earlier completed six of thirteen stages, retained 557,737 observations and reused 108 historical targets. These dated outcomes stay in the evidence history. Recovery and a prepared repair do not turn any failed owner into a completed run.</p><p>The earlier B033 attempt restored its parent, built historical features and completed all 108 registered target fits across the two leagues. A shared-summary selector then encountered a summary belonging to another project and stopped the current-source refresh. The incomplete refresh produced no fresh current-game or provider coverage. The committed historical artifacts and the verified return remain preserved.</p><p>B035 later stopped before science with 510 passed fixtures, three errors and one skip. B036 corrected that portability problem and completed the workflow. It still recorded 417 current boxscore normalization errors, exchange identity gaps, a Kalshi rate-limit halt, and no configured runtime historical-odds credential. The earlier B032 attempt had failed at the streaming-reader boundary with zero completed scientific stages. That failure remains in the evidence history. Its later durability verification did not add scientific credit. The B033 stream repair allowed real work to proceed; neither repair nor test success implies full coverage or a market advantage.</p></details>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="research-status" aria-labelledby="research-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Research in preparation</div><h2 id="research-title">Coverage first. Claims after measurement.</h2></div><p>B043 acquired injury evidence but did not complete its injury comparison or reach the path study. B044 stopped at the source handoff. B045 continuation is prepared; no measured gain is asserted.</p></div><div class="track-grid"><article class="track"><span class="badge">INJURY STUDY · CHECKPOINT FAILED</span><h3>Injury evidence and forecast time</h3><p id="injury-copy"></p><p class="table-note" id="injury-clocks"></p><p class="table-note" id="injury-policy"></p></article><article class="track"><span class="badge">MARKET PATHS · NOT REACHED</span><h3>Chronological market-path research</h3><p id="frontier-copy"></p><p class="table-note" id="frontier-limit"></p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="engineering" aria-labelledby="engineering-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect the engineering</div><h2 id="engineering-title">Move a clock. Watch the contract.</h2></div><p>This interaction uses invented inputs only. The executable Python example tests the same classes of failure without credentials, subscriptions or cloud access.</p></div><div class="engineering"><div class="panel"><h3>Information available before 16:00 UTC</h3><p class="subtle">Invented tipoff: 18:00 UTC · decision horizon: two hours.</p><div class="demo-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented contract scenarios"><button type="button" data-scenario="valid" aria-pressed="true">All inputs in time</button><button type="button" data-scenario="late_quote" aria-pressed="false">Late quote</button><button type="button" data-scenario="boundary_label" aria-pressed="false">Boundary label</button><button type="button" data-scenario="settlement" aria-pressed="false">Wrong settlement</button></div><div class="demo-clocks"><div><span>Latest training label</span><strong id="demo-label">15:00 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Quote available</span><strong id="demo-quote">15:55 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Feature available</span><strong>15:10 UTC</strong></div><div><span>Settlement scope</span><strong id="demo-settlement">Full game + overtime</strong></div></div><div class="demo-output" id="demo-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><p class="table-note">Passing a comparison contract does not authorize a wager. The public payoff example separately requires explicit price and fee evidence and always emits zero orders.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Reproduce the review mechanism.</h3><p class="subtle">Python 3.11+ · standard library · deterministic invented data.</p><pre class="code">python examples/ncaa_review/contracts.py --demo
python examples/ncaa_review/progress.py
python examples/ncaa_review/handoff.py --demo
python -m unittest discover -s examples/ncaa_review -p 'test_*.py'
python examples/ncaa_review/build_dashboard.py --check</pre><ul class="checklist"><li>Reject future and exact-boundary training labels.</li><li>Pair each provider on the exact same games and products.</li><li>Keep frozen, reconstructed and issued tracks separate.</li><li>Preserve both winning and losing disagreements.</li><li>Verify complete streamed bytes and close the actual reader.</li></ul><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/tree/main/examples/ncaa_review">Read the source, tests and methodology ↗</a></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="progress" aria-labelledby="progress-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">04 / Invented progress contract</div><h2 id="progress-title">An estimate needs evidence.</h2></div><p>Switch the invented scenario to inspect counts and a measured phase ETA. This is a reproducible demonstration, not a connection to a running owner workload.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="demo-buttons progress-buttons" id="progress-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented progress scenarios"></div><div class="progress-demo-grid"><div><span class="progress-key">Durably completed units</span><div class="progress-count" id="progress-count"></div><div class="progress-track" id="progress-track" role="progressbar" aria-label="Invented task completion"><span id="progress-fill"></span></div><div class="progress-subline" id="progress-components"></div></div><div id="progress-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"><span class="progress-key">Estimated time remaining in this phase</span><div class="progress-eta" id="progress-eta"></div><div class="progress-range" id="progress-range"></div><div class="progress-subline" id="progress-clocks" style="margin-top:12px"></div></div></div><p class="progress-note" id="progress-explanation"></p><p class="table-note">Restored units reduce remaining work without inflating new-work throughput. Unknown totals, warmup, a changed worker count or a stalled pace produce an explicit unavailable estimate. A measured pace range is not a confidence interval or a promise about later phases.</p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/progress.py">Inspect the executable progress contract ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="preflight" aria-labelledby="preflight-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">05 / Invented portable validation</div><h2 id="preflight-title">Finished checks are not all passes.</h2></div><p>Unsupported optional integration, required capability and unexpected errors have different outcomes. No process, provider or model is accessed by this example.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="demo-buttons" id="preflight-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Invented preflight scenarios"></div><div class="demo-output" id="preflight-output" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div><div class="coverage-grid" id="preflight-counts"></div><p class="table-note" id="preflight-explanation"></p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/preflight.py">Inspect the portable validation contract ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="section" id="handoff" aria-labelledby="handoff-title"><div class="section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">06 / Invented provenance contract</div><h2 id="handoff-title">Test the handoff itself.</h2></div><p>A producer and a consumer can each pass their own tests while their actual handoff remains incompatible. Validate their exact shared contract before work begins.</p></div><div class="panel"><div class="data-scroll"><table><caption>Invented results generated by the executable example</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Observed result</th></tr></thead><tbody id="handoff-table"></tbody></table></div><p class="table-note">The reviewed registration binds project, release, run, source digest, canonical artifact prefix, wire format and exact content pins. Mixed identities, conflicting registrations and rehashed payload substitutions are rejected. This example assumes an authenticated registry and supplies no private owner or model evidence.</p><a href="https://github.com/alvaromendizabal/sports-edge-lab/blob/main/examples/ncaa_review/handoff.py">Inspect the handoff contract and adversarial tests ↗</a></div></section>
